Subject: [PATCH 5/6] docs(cookbook): use the SM90 MXFP4 W4A8 MoE kernel in
 DeepSeek-V4 H200 cells

Switch the three H200 + FP4 low-latency single-node cells (flash-official,
flash, pro) to the new W4A8 path -- MXFP4 weights x FP8 activations via
FlashInfer's Humming kernels:

    --moe-runner-backend flashinfer_mxfp4
    --flashinfer-mxfp4-moe-precision fp8

flash-official and flash previously ran Marlin W4A16; pro already used the
FlashInfer W4A16 runner and only gains the precision flag. The cells carry
verificationStatus: "in-progress" until they are re-benchmarked with the
new kernel, and a comment records the FlashInfer >= 0.6.18 requirement and
the W4A16 fallbacks. Balanced / high-throughput cells are left on their
verified W4A16 commands for now.

Update the Hopper note in the MDX page accordingly: FP4 on Hopper is no
longer W4A16-only; the W4A8 opt-in and its version requirement are
documented, and the low-latency cells are called out as generating the
new form.

The MoE backend card is deliberately unchanged: backend-option requiresHw
filtering only applies to the MegaMoE entry, so a card-level W4A8 option
would be offered on Blackwell where --flashinfer-mxfp4-moe-precision fp8
raises by design.
